Port patch 0013 - look up font glyph indices in the glyph table by name
Why: Font_MapGlyphCode reads the glyph table D_8006F650 only by indexing past the end of the display-list arrays gUiRestoreTextureDL
(code 0x20..0x7F) and D_8006F608 (code 0xA0..0xFF), relying on the original linker placing the table right behind them. Nothing else
references the table, so the native compiler drops it and the lookups read unrelated data: all on-screen text was garbled (found by
running the game, confirmed with nm). The table is now non-static and indexed directly with the same indices as the original layout
(code - 0x20, and 0x60 + code - 0xA0; the US table has 0xC0 entries). Behaviour on the original build is unchanged.

--- a/src/ui_graphics.c
+++ b/src/ui_graphics.c
@@ -147,7 sha256=c853b183d00188393591c872245078f3cb632875b593739b2e22c606563f1cb9 @@
=3
-1
+/* PORT: not static, and declared in graphics_textures.c. Font_MapGlyphCode reaches this table only through an overrun of the
+ * preceding display-list arrays, so nothing else referenced it and the native compiler dropped it (see port patch 0013). */
+u8 D_8006F650[] = {
=3
--- a/src/graphics_textures.c
+++ b/src/graphics_textures.c
@@ -302,13 sha256=33a2e3d3f8ad201d86d5d1c1c34a911dba93ccfacb0f5ffa7b1453a4884eefa1 @@
=3
+/* PORT: the original code indexes past the end of the display-list arrays gUiRestoreTextureDL and D_8006F608, relying on the
+ * linker having placed the glyph table D_8006F650 right behind them (D_8006F650 = gUiRestoreTextureDL + 0x20 and
+ * D_8006F608 + sizeof(Gfx) + 0xA0 = D_8006F650 + 0x60). Nothing else references the table, so the native compiler discards it and the
+ * lookup read unrelated data (garbled text). Index the table by name instead; the indices are the same as in the original layout. */
+extern u8 D_8006F650[];
+
=4
-1
+        var_v1 = D_8006F650[arg0 - 0x20];
=1
-1
+        var_v1 = D_8006F650[0x60 + (arg0 - 0xA0)];
=3
